Python Lists — Fundamentals
This section introduces lists, one of Python's fundamental data structures.
Concepts Covered
Creating lists
Accessing elements using indexes
Positive and negative indexing
Adding elements with append()
Updating list elements
Finding list length with len()
List mutability
Objective
Understand how to store, access, and modify multiple values using Python lists.
Practice File
lists_fundamentals.py
Key Takeaway
Lists are ordered, mutable collections that can store multiple values. Indexing starts at 0, and negative indexes access elements from the end.
